{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795390279,"nonce":"Ud6fSGjmGJpyO+GbvJpDT+LF4W4=","title":"jno.fem: a varying coefficient times a boundary normal in a vector surface term is wrong at the default quadrature","message":"Found on feat/fvm. inner(c * nr, phi.bind(x=xr, y=yr), n_contract=1) with c a coordinate (yr) or a P1 field parameter, on a 2-D vector P1 field: the solution differs from the same problem at quad_degree=4 by O(1) (2.8 against a solution of 0.4); a constant c is right. Likely the per-quadrature-point coefficient (n_q,) is multiplied elementwise with the per-facet normal (dim,) when n_q == dim == 2, instead of as (n_q, 1) * (dim,). Workaround in jno/_coupling: a vector interface load is written componentwise, c * n[..., k] * phi[k].","files":null}]}